    "body": "> This section is specifically talking about an `<img>` element.\r\n\r\nThat does not appear to be clear according to the actual text of the specification, at\r\n\r\n> If the element [represents](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#represents) an image\r\n\r\nand \r\n\r\n> If the element does not [represent](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#represents) an image\r\n\r\nWhat are examples of the two cases?\r\n\r\n1. \"represents an image\"; and\r\n2. \"does not represent an image\"",
