    "body": "> That does not appear to be clear according to the actual text of the specification\r\n\r\nUh... the relevant section is explicitly about \"img elements and input elements whose type attributes are in the Image Button state\".  So ok, not just `<img>`, but definitely not `<picture>`.\r\n\r\n> What are examples of the two cases?\r\n\r\nSee https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-img-element and search for \"What an img element represents depends on the src attribute and the alt attribute\".  Spec has no way to link directly there, unfortunately.\r\n\r\nSimilarly, see <https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#image-button-state-(type=image)> and search for \"The element represents\".  Again, no way to link there, and it's not super-readable.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
