    "created_at": "2018-04-09T13:43:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-09T13:43:38Z",
    "body": "Ah, sorry, I should have made that clearer.\r\n\r\nIn my quick testing, I don't think there is any browser where CSS width/height affect the type of box.  There are just different behaviors for the \"no alt\" case in terms of what type of box is created to start with.\r\n\r\nThe right way to proceed is definitely to write a bunch of tests for all the cases here, in both standards and quirks mode, and then see what browsers actually do with them.  One can use an empty `<span>` as a reftest for \"empty inline\" and an `<svg width=\"0\" height=\"0\">` as a reftest for \"0x0 intrinsic size replaced element\", I think...",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
